        { "key": "tut_01", "value": "Welcome to the best <size=50%><color=grey>(and only)</color></size> government-approved game engine." },
        { "key": "tut_02", "value": "To develop your game, you have to place the components from the <color=#06EF06>grid</color> on the left" },
        { "key": "tut_03", "value": "so that they fit without leaving any gaps in the <color=red>grid</color> on the right." },
        { "key": "tut_04", "value": "Each component has its properties, which will be displayed when selecting the component on the <color=orange>screen</color>." },
        { "key": "tut_05", "value": "Every game needs 4 components: <color=purple>Mechanics</color>, <color=#946B1F>Genre</color>, <color=#E5C16F>Style</color> and an <color=#5D69A9>Item</color>. You will know which is which by the screen or by the color of the component." },
        { "key": "tut_06", "value": "To move the components you just have to <size=90%><b>click</b></size> on them. Once selected you can rotate them with the <size=90%><b>Q</b></size> and <size=90%><b>E</b></size> keys." },
        { "key": "tut_07", "value": "and move them with the <size=90%><b>W</b></size>, <size=90%><b>A</b></size>, <size=90%><b>S</b></size>, <size=90%><b>D</b></size> keys." },
        { "key": "tut_08", "value": "To confirm the position of the components on the grid use the <size=90%><b>space bar</b></size>" },
        { "key": "tut_09", "value": "and if you change your mind you can return the component to the grid on the left with the <size=90%><b>right click</b></size> while you have it selected." },
        { "key": "tut_10", "value": "Good luck." },
        { "key": "tut_angry", "value": "<size=120%><color=red>STOP IT!</color></size>\nDON'T YOU SEE YOU CAN'T PLACE IT THERE?" },

        { "key": "error_83_title", "value": "ERROR(83): GridNotFull"},
        { "key": "error_83_message", "value": "The grid is still not full. \nPlease, complete it before sending."},
